# The SDK's files under the path that names their version (its two bundles and,
# P84, the head script) never change once released, so a browser keeps them for
# a year without asking again. Every other path, the unversioned SDK paths
# included, keeps the asset default: revalidated on each use. The rules name the
# files exactly, so no other answer under /sdk/ can carry the header. The
# deploy's package step accepts only these rules (scripts/stamp-workflow.mjs); a
# new SDK version changes the paths.
/sdk/0.2.0/edge-personalization.esm.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/sdk/0.2.0/edge-personalization.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/sdk/0.2.0/edge-head.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
